        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "bd0c6c3a-1fb8-5879-9924-3c14483500eb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Savenac Nursery Historic District, Haugan, Mineral County, Montana, northeast Washington, northern Idaho, western Montana, Rocky Mountains, western United States\n- People: Elers Koch\n- Organizations: Forest Service\n- Events: Great Fire of 1910, Big Blowup, Big Burn, Devil's Broom fire\n- Topics: wildfire, nursery creation, fire damage\n\nFacts:\n- Savenac Nursery Historic District is located near Haugan in Mineral County, Montana.\n- Elers Koch of the Forest Service created the nursery at Savenac Nursery Historic District.\n- In 1910, the Great Fire of 1910 was a wildfire in the western United States.\n- The Great Fire of 1910 is also commonly called the Big Blowup, the Big Burn, or the Devil's Broom fire.\n- The Great Fire of 1910 burned about 3,000,000 acres in northeast Washington, northern Idaho, and western Montana.\n- Elers Koch helped fight the Great Fire of 1910.\n- The Great Fire of 1910 destroyed much of the northern Rocky Mountains, including the nursery.",
